    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0115" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-12">12 January 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    Leahy to President:</p>
                <p>The following draft reply to Harriman’s
                    messages of January 11 is forwarded for your consideration:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Receipt is acknowledged of your . . . [five telegrams dated January
                            11].<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/>
                    </p>
                    <pb facs="0116" n="34" xml:id="pg34"/>
                    <p>I will be pleased to see you at Malta and learn from you of the latest
                        developments in your area.</p>
                    <p>I expect to depart Malta for 
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Argonaut</hi>
                         February second.</p>
                    <p>
                        Stettinius will not visit Moscow
                        prior to or immediately following 
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Argonaut</hi>.</p>
                    <p>It is not considered advisable for you to urge Stalin to bring his military staff with him. He will
                        undoubtedly bring those that he wants without urging by us.”<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d52-f2"/>
                    </p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">illiam</hi>] D.
                                L[<hi rendition="#small-caps">eahy</hi>]
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="1" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>One of the telegrams under reference is the message printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>. Another has not been found. The other three
                    dealt with identification cards for Americans going to Yalta living
                    accommodations at Yalta, and the travel arrangements referred to in Leahy’s drafts reply.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f2" n="2" xml:id="d52-f2-content">
                <p>It is not known whether this proposed message was sent by Roosevelt to Harriman.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
